WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Campus Access coordinates vehicle entry
across every gate from one system.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
It connects hosts, security teams, and
administrators around one shared workflow.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The command center brings gate status, queues,
arrivals, reviews, and device health together.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
An interactive campus map makes each entry point
directly accessible while exceptions stay visible.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
At each gate, plate candidates and confidence sit
beside camera state and matching access context.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Operators can inspect the evidence, understand the
match, and keep the gate action deliberate.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Hosts create structured requests with vehicle, site,
gate, purpose, and a bounded time window.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Reviewers work from a prioritized queue, so a decision
becomes a searchable record—not a lost email.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
The operations view connects incidents and device
health to gate, severity, owner, and recency.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Degraded cameras and unresolved events remain visible
without pushing active arrivals out of view.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Administrators configure tenant identity, campus
topology, gate devices, locale, time zone, and API.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Those choices remain configuration, keeping the
product reusable without campus-specific forks.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.000
The same console adapts to booth and mobile widths
without splitting the workflow across separate apps.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:39.000
English, French, and Arabic right-to-left layouts
are built into the interface.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:46.000
A typed FastAPI control plane persists tenant-scoped
workflows behind the console.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:53.000
The versioned inference boundary and explicit edge
integration seams keep each responsibility replaceable.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.000
The result is a runnable platform slice:

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.000
multi-gate operations, structured access, AI evidence,
tests, runbooks, and reproducible delivery.
